  message: "Fixed in PR #1782. tests/tui_pilot.click waits until the target is the widget get_widget_at() finds at the exact click point, then clicks and raises if the click did not land; all 84 pilot.click sites in test_tui.py and test_item_nav_modal.py use it. Evidence: (1) TestClickWhenClickable, under wait_for_idle patched to return at once: a plain pilot.click on #cancel returns False and the modal is never dismissed; the helper lands on #cancel and #submit. (2) The same model applied to every test in both files: unmodified dev 20 failed, 11 of them modal click tests including the nightly's failing test_it_returns_the_result_under_the_one_tick_model[#submit]; with the fix those 11 pass and no new test fails. Unstarved: 580 passed."  # fcfd
